RAII is not a specific syntax but a design pattern.  It's implemented by ensuring that resource acquisition happens in the constructor and release in the destructor.  For example:

```c++
class FileOpener {
public:
    FileOpener(const std::string& filename) : file_(filename) {
        if (!file_.is_open()) {
            throw std::runtime_error("Could not open file");
        }
    }
    ~FileOpener() { file_.close(); }
    // ... other methods ...
private:
    std::fstream file_;
};
```

**Note:** The `std::fstream` destructor automatically handles closing the file, even if exceptions are thrown.
